The Android package does not ship Cloudflare's official linux-arm64 release.
That binary is a non-PIE ET_EXEC, which Android refuses to execute. Quick Temp Open Server
rebuilds the tag recorded in third_party/CLOUDFLARED_VERSION with:

    CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=android GOARCH=arm64 go build -trimpath -buildmode=pie

For that build only, third_party/android_dns.go is copied to
cmd/cloudflared/android_dns.go. It points the Go resolver at public DNS
servers because Android has no usable /etc/resolv.conf. It is not an upstream
cloudflared change.

Try Cloudflare Quick Tunnels (https://*.trycloudflare.com) are for testing and
development. They are not named Cloudflare Tunnels and are not a production
hosting service.
